msgid "Connecting with ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:7
#: 73f6083d66ad4c5e82985dd3a4f564d0
msgid "Before attempting to connect with ROS, ensure that the physical serial cable connection and ArduPilot side parameters have been set as described on the appropriate companion computer page (:ref:`RPi3 <raspberry-pi-via-mavlink>`, :ref:`NVidia TX1 <companion-computer-nvidia-tx1>`, :ref:`NVidia TX2 <companion-computer-nvidia-tx2>` or :ref:`Intel Edison <intel-edison>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:9
#: b083a92582ee43e98c943a94362c18f6
msgid "The connection between ArduPilot running on the flight controller and ROS/MAVROS can be established with the following commands on the companion computer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:11
#: 46a9f877f0cd40a59e679ff7c50e5841
msgid "open up a terminal and type, \"roscore\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:12
#: 3f621a13e3474469b32182031034b502
msgid "open another terminal and start mavros as described `here on the ros/mavros wiki <http://wiki.ros.org/mavros#Usage>`__.  For example, the following instruction is appropriate for a TX2/APSync install with port 14855 opened (see \"How flight controller data is routed to various programs\" at the bottom of :ref:`this page <apsync-intro>`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:18
#: 7daf2d705b26487d9933fe5a7e064893
msgid "Test the flight controller is responding to `mavros commands <http://wiki.ros.org/mavros#Utility_commands>`__ like `mavsys <http://wiki.ros.org/mavros#mavsys>`__ (which can set the flight mode) and `mavsafety <http://wiki.ros.org/mavros#mavsafety>`__ (which can arm/disarm the vehicle):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-connecting.rst:27
#: f93fa18c2ec54a2e877b2fc9320777eb
msgid "We are keen to improve ArduPilot's support of ROS so if you find issues (such as commands that do not seem to be supported), please report them in the `ArduPilot issues list <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues>`__ with a title that includes \"ROS\" and we will attempt to resolve them as quickly as possible."
msgstr ""
